    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence is genuinely balanced between the bull and bear cases. The long-term trend remains intact \u2014 price is 12.5% above a rising 200-day SMA ($156.87), the 50-day SMA is rising ($182.26), and Q1 2024 operating cash flow was robust at $18.99B with a strong balance sheet. However, the short-term momentum is clearly negative: price is below the 10 EMA ($181.18), 50 SMA ($182.26), Bollinger lower band ($177.41), and VWMA ($182.79), with MACD negative (-0.72) and expanding for 12 consecutive days, and RSI at 36.75 still falling and not yet oversold. There is no confirmation of a bottom (no bullish divergence, no MACD contraction, no close back above the lower Bollinger Band), so adding is premature. But the intact long-term uptrend and strong cash generation argue against a full exit. This is a textbook Hold: maintain existing exposure at ~$176.44, do not add until at least two bottom-confirmation signals appear (close above $177.41, MACD histogram contraction, RSI reclaiming 40, or bullish RSI divergence), and trim only on a decisive daily close below the 200-day SMA ($156.87).\n\n**Entry Price**: 176.44\n\n**Stop Loss**: 170.7\n\n**Position Sizing**: Neutral/benchmark weight, no more than ~5% of portfolio\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
